    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-36b-ss-1 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Minister may determine in writing that a person aged 14 or older ceases to be an Australian citizen if the Minister is satisfied that:  (a) the person:  (i) engaged in conduct specified in subsection (5) while outside Australia; or  (ii) engaged in conduct specified in any of paragraphs (5)(a) to (h) while in Australia, has since left Australia and has not been tried for an offence in relation to the conduct; and  (b) the conduct demonstrates that the person has repudiated their allegiance to Australia; and  (c) it would be contrary to the public interest for the person to remain an Australian citizen (see section 36E).  Amendments  Schedule 1 Amendments  Part 1  No. 88, 2020 Australian Citizenship Amendment (Citizenship Cessation) Act 2020  Note: A person may seek review of a determination made under this subsection in the High Court of Australia under section 75 of the Constitution, or in the Federal Court of Australia under section 39B of the Judiciary Act 1903. See also section 36H of this Act (revocation of citizenship cessation determination on application to Minister)." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Minister may determine in writing that a person aged 14 or older ceases to be an Australian citizen if the Minister is satisfied that:  (a) the person:  (i) engaged in conduct specified in subsection (5) while outside Australia; or  (ii) engaged in conduct specified in any of paragraphs (5)(a) to (h) while in Australia, has since left Australia and has not been tried for an offence in relation to the conduct; and  (b) the conduct demonstrates that the person has repudiated their allegiance to Australia; and  (c) it would be contrary to the public interest for the person to remain an Australian citizen (see section 36E).  Amendments  Schedule 1 Amendments  Part 1  No. 88, 2020 Australian Citizenship Amendment (Citizenship Cessation) Act 2020  Note: A person may seek review of a determination made under this subsection in the High Court of Australia under section 75 of the Constitution, or in the Federal Court of Australia under section 39B of the Judiciary Act 1903. See also section 36H of this Act (revocation of citizenship cessation determination on application to Minister)."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "605418e9e211c824d5f527f6f0b57b4c1d2c2b8d3e8f3de83b3b700e2fdc1d2e" ;
    values:partOf concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-citizenship-cessation-act-2020-sch-1-sec-36b ;
    cof:pageNumber "8"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Ceases to be an Australian citizen if engages in specified conduct while outside or in Australia, has repudiated allegiance, and it would be contrary to public interest." ;
