    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "Section 36D of the amended Act applies in relation to a conviction of a person:  (a) that occurs after commencement; or  (b) that occurred before commencement, if:  (i) the conviction occurred on or after 29 May 2003; and  (ii) the person was sentenced to a period of imprisonment of at least 3 years, or to periods of imprisonment that total at least 3 years, in respect of the conviction." ;
    cof:pageNumber "28"^^xsd:integer .

concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-citizenship-cessation-act-2020-sch-1-sec-20 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "20 Declared terrorist organisations"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-20 ;
    values:originalText "Despite the repeal of section 35AA of the Act by this Schedule, a declaration in force under that section immediately before commencement continues in force, after commencement, as if it had been made under section 36C of the amended Act." ;
    skos:definition "Despite the repeal of section 35AA of the Act by this Schedule, a declaration in force under that section immediately before commencement continues in force, after commencement, as if it had been made under section 36C of the amended Act."@en ;
